<title>USA: Marion Capital sets stock buyback program.</title>
<headline>Marion Capital sets stock buyback program.</headline>
<dateline>MARION, Ind. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marion Capital Holdings Inc said Tuesday its board approved the repurchase of five percent of the company's outstanding shares, or up to 92,207 shares, from time to time on the open market.</p>
<p>It said the board authorized an expenditure of up to $2 million for the buyback program.</p>
<p>Marion Capital, holding company for First Federal Savings Bank of Marion, has completed six similar stock repurchase programs since converting to stock form on March 18, 1993.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
